The two Most used regexes in my program are:
INT_VARIABLE - 
"\\s*((final)\\s+)?int\\s+(([a-zA-Z]|_\\w)\\w*)
(\\s*,\\s*((([a-zA-Z]|_\\w)\\w*))
|\\s*=\\s*([+-]?\\d+|(([a-zA-Z]|_\\w)\\w*)))*
(\\s*);\\s*"

This regex is mostly been used for 
checking variable declarations of type int.
 Ive chopped specifically in by I could choose any
 of the five variables (int, string, char, boolean and double)
 as I used them a lot. Explanation of the regex structure:
1. At the start of the regex we look for a final word and group it.
This is optional by using ?
2‪.‬ At the second part we check if there is an int
3‪.‬ After it, we check if the variable name is legal.
4‪.‬ After checking the variable name.
 We check if there are either more variables
 to declare (separated by comma) and if they are initialized. 
5‪.‬ At the end, we check for an ending line sign (;)

  
METHOD_DECLARTION - \s*void\s*
(([a-zA-Z])\w*)\s*\
(\s*(()|((final)\s+)?(String|int|double|boolean|char)
\s+(([a-zA-Z]|_\w)\w*)(\s*,\s*(((final)\s+)?
(String|int|double|boolean|char)\s+(([a-zA-Z]|_\w)\w*)))*)
\s*\)\s*\{\s* 
(took from debug mode for full regex, so \\ is replaced with \)

This regex is being used to check for method declaration
 in the program. Explanation of the regex structure:
1‪.‬ Checks for void at the start of the line. (Mandatory)
2‪.‬ Check for a legal name for a function
3‪.‬starting to check for parameters of method inside its ().
 Could be either a method that doesn't get a parameter
 or that gets a couple of parameters 
(each parameter can be from a different type). 
Also, each parameter can be a final one.
 Parameters don't get a value in method declaration. 
4‪.‬ Checking for a start block '{' after ()     
  